sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Web/Mobile Client
    participant Filter as JwtAuthFilter (iam)
    participant TenantFilter as TenantContextFilter (tenancy)
    participant Service as Module Service (e.g. parking)
    participant Hibernate as Hibernate Tenant Filter
    participant PG as PostgreSQL (RLS enabled)

    Client->>Filter: HTTP request, Authorization: Bearer JWT
    Filter->>Filter: verify signature (HS256), check expiry
    Filter-->>TenantFilter: authenticated principal (userId, role, tenant_id, site_ids[])
    TenantFilter->>TenantFilter: set ThreadLocal TenantContext(tenant_id, siteIds)
    TenantFilter->>PG: open connection, SET LOCAL app.tenant_id = '<tenant_id>'
    TenantFilter->>Service: proceed with filter chain
    Service->>Hibernate: enable filter "tenantFilter" with param tenant_id
    Service->>PG: SELECT ... (Hibernate appends WHERE tenant_id = :tenantId)
    PG->>PG: RLS policy re-checks USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::uuid)
    PG-->>Service: rows (only current tenant's, double-enforced)
    Service-->>Client: response

    Note over TenantFilter,PG: If site_id is required for the endpoint and the JWT's<br/>site_ids[] does not include the requested siteId, reject 403<br/>before touching the database.
    Note over TenantFilter: ThreadLocal + RLS session var are cleared at request end<br/>(finally block) to prevent leakage across pooled connections/threads.
